# Harness (orchestrator rules)

Source of truth for paths, CLIs and templates: `docs/harness/README.md`. Terms: `docs/glossary.md`. Do not copy them here.

## Respond directly (no pipeline)
Answering questions, or editing docs/plans the user explicitly asked for. No subagents, no run-state.

## Classify the lane (smallest that fits)
- XS: docs/config/one-liner. S: 1-3 files, no interface change. M: new feature or interface change. L: a whole phase (several M runs).
- Docs-only changes skip the judge. When unsure between two lanes, pick the smaller; escalate by evidence, not by guess.

## Task packet
Build it once from `docs/harness/templates/task-packet.md`: goal, lane, spec excerpts, lessons filtered by tag, explorer paths, acceptance criteria, check command, budget remaining. Subagents see only the packet; do not make them re-explore.

## Run state
- `node scripts/harness/run-state.mjs init|transition|call|status` for every state change and subagent call.
- States: intake, plan, execute, check, debug, judge, done, escalate. Never skip or bounce back.
- Exit code 3 (budget exceeded) or `escalate`: stop and report to the user. Never retry past a cap.
- Caps: executor 2 check attempts, debugger 3 attempts, planner 2 explorer calls, judge 1 run.

## Waves
- Contract step (serial) freezes shared files; fan-out tasks fill only their own `owns:` paths; integration (serial) merges.
- Docs/config waves share the checkout with disjoint paths. Code waves: one worktree + branch `task/<task-id>` per task, max 5 code agents at once.
- Register `run-state.mjs claim <task>` before launching; overlapping claims are refused. Release after merge.
- One planner call and one judge run per wave. Debugger only for the failed task, in its worktree.
- Integration: merge in dependency order, `check full` after each merge, `ownership-check.mjs`, then judge. A failed branch is held back as `wip/<task-id>`; the rest still merges.

## Shared files
Only contract/integration steps edit: codemap, spec, `FioreEvent` enum + TS mirror, registries, `reactions/index.ts`, `sensors/mod.rs`, atlas loader. Executors report deviations instead.

## Lessons
Subagents return candidates only. You are the sole writer of `docs/harness/lessons.md`: append tagged, dedupe, cap ~80 entries.

## Harness changes
Edits to `.cursor/agents|rules|skills|hooks` or `docs/harness/*` (except lessons) need an approved proposal in `.harness/proposals/` and an `/eval` run.

## Git
- `main` gets only judged checkpoint commits (conventional commits). Push after integration.
- Never `git push --force`, `git reset --hard`, or push `task/*` to `main`. `CURSOR_API_KEY` from env only; never commit secrets.
- Privacy: never read keystroke content; no window titles/track names in logs above debug level.
